Explanation of Your MySQL Config
Connection & Files
Parameter	Meaning
socket	Unix socket file used for local client connections
log-error	Error log location (startup issues, crashes, warnings)
pid-file	Stores the mysqld process ID
server_id=7	Unique ID of this server. Mandatory for replication and binlog; must be different on every server in a replication topology
Read/Write Mode
Parameter	Meaning
read_only=off	Normal users with write privileges can write
super_read_only=off	Even SUPER users can write. Set both to ON on replicas to prevent accidental writes
Binary Logging
Parameter	Meaning
log-bin = mysql-bin	Enables binary logs (used for replication and point-in-time recovery)
log-bin-index	Index file listing all binlog files
binlog_format = ROW	Logs actual row changes. Safest for replication, though larger in size
##expire_logs_days = 7	Commented out, so binlogs never auto-delete and disk can fill up. In MySQL 8 use binlog_expire_logs_seconds instead
Memory / Packet
Parameter	Meaning
tmp_table_size = 2048M	Max size of in-memory temp tables before spilling to disk. Per connection, so 2GB is very risky with many connections
max_allowed_packet = 1024M	Max size of a single query/packet (large BLOBs, bulk inserts). 1GB is the maximum
bulk_insert_buffer_size = 1G	Cache for bulk inserts into MyISAM. Mostly irrelevant for InnoDB; 1G is excessive
SQL Mode

sql_mode="STRICT_TRANS_TABLES,NO_ZERO_IN_DATE,NO_ZERO_DATE,ERROR_FOR_DIVISION_BY_ZERO,NO_ENGINE_SUBSTITUTION"

STRICT_TRANS_TABLES: errors on invalid data instead of silently truncating
NO_ZERO_IN_DATE / NO_ZERO_DATE: rejects dates like 2024-00-10 or 0000-00-00
ERROR_FOR_DIVISION_BY_ZERO: error on divide by zero
NO_ENGINE_SUBSTITUTION: error if the requested storage engine is unavailable

(The other # lines are old commented alternatives.)

Slow Query Log
Parameter	Meaning
slow_query_log=1	Enable slow query logging
slow_query_log_file	Where it is written
long_query_time = 5	Queries taking more than 5 seconds are logged. Consider 1–2 sec for tuning
Authentication
Parameter	Meaning
mysql_native_password=ON	Enables the legacy auth plugin (disabled by default in MySQL 8.4+, removed in 9.x). Needed for older clients
Connections
Parameter	Meaning
max_connections = 1000	Max simultaneous client connections
InnoDB
Parameter	Meaning
innodb_buffer_pool_size = 24G	Memory cache for data and indexes. The most important setting; typically 50–70% of RAM on a dedicated DB server
innodb_open_files = 400	Max .ibd files InnoDB keeps open at once. Low if you have many tables
innodb_io_capacity = 400	IOPS InnoDB assumes for background tasks (flushing). Set according to disk type (HDD ~200, SSD 2000+, NVMe higher)
innodb_flush_method = O_DIRECT	Bypasses OS cache to avoid double buffering. Recommended on Linux
innodb_read_io_threads / write_io_threads = 8	Threads for background read and write I/O
innodb_log_file_size = 2G	Size of each redo log file. Larger gives better write performance but longer crash recovery (deprecated in 8.0.30+ in favor of innodb_redo_log_capacity)
Parameters to Add for a Newly Created MySQL Server

Here is a solid baseline my.cnf (adjust values to your RAM/disk):

ini
[mysqld]
# --- Basic ---
datadir                 = /var/lib/mysql
socket                  = /var/lib/mysql/mysql.sock
port                    = 3306
bind-address            = 0.0.0.0        # or specific IP
user                    = mysql
skip-name-resolve                         # faster connections, use IPs in grants
character-set-server    = utf8mb4
collation-server        = utf8mb4_unicode_ci
default-time-zone       = '+05:30'        # or '+00:00' (UTC recommended)
lower_case_table_names  = 1               # only set at initialization time!

# --- Logging ---
log-error               = /var/log/mysqld.log
slow_query_log          = 1
slow_query_log_file     = /var/lib/mysql/mysql-slow.log
long_query_time         = 2
log_queries_not_using_indexes = 0         # enable temporarily when tuning
log_error_verbosity     = 3

# --- Binary log / replication ---
server_id               = 1               # unique per server
log-bin                 = mysql-bin
binlog_format           = ROW
binlog_expire_logs_seconds = 604800       # 7 days (MySQL 8)
sync_binlog             = 1               # durability
max_binlog_size         = 512M
gtid_mode               = ON              # recommended for replication
enforce_gtid_consistency = ON
log_replica_updates     = ON              # (log_slave_updates in 5.7)
# On replicas:
# read_only = ON
# super_read_only = ON
# relay_log_recovery = ON

# --- Connections ---
max_connections         = 500
max_connect_errors      = 100000
wait_timeout            = 600
interactive_timeout     = 600
thread_cache_size       = 100
back_log                = 512

# --- Per-session buffers (keep small!) ---
sort_buffer_size        = 2M
join_buffer_size        = 2M
read_buffer_size        = 1M
read_rnd_buffer_size    = 2M
tmp_table_size          = 128M
max_heap_table_size     = 128M            # keep equal to tmp_table_size
max_allowed_packet      = 256M

# --- Table caches ---
table_open_cache        = 4000
table_definition_cache  = 2000
open_files_limit        = 65535

# --- InnoDB ---
default_storage_engine          = InnoDB
innodb_buffer_pool_size         = 24G     # ~60-70% of RAM
innodb_buffer_pool_instances    = 8       # 1 per GB, max 8-16
innodb_log_file_size            = 2G      # or innodb_redo_log_capacity=4G (8.0.30+)
innodb_log_buffer_size          = 64M
innodb_flush_log_at_trx_commit  = 1       # full ACID; 2 = faster, small risk
innodb_flush_method             = O_DIRECT
innodb_file_per_table           = 1
innodb_io_capacity              = 2000    # SSD
innodb_io_capacity_max          = 4000
innodb_read_io_threads          = 8
innodb_write_io_threads         = 8
innodb_open_files               = 4000
innodb_lock_wait_timeout        = 50
innodb_buffer_pool_dump_at_shutdown = 1
innodb_buffer_pool_load_at_startup  = 1

# --- Security / SQL mode ---
sql_mode = STRICT_TRANS_TABLES,NO_ZERO_IN_DATE,NO_ZERO_DATE,ERROR_FOR_DIVISION_BY_ZERO,NO_ENGINE_SUBSTITUTION
local_infile              = 0
# default_authentication_plugin = caching_sha2_password (default in 8.0)

# --- Optional monitoring ---
performance_schema      = ON

[client]
socket                  = /var/lib/mysql/mysql.sock
default-character-set   = utf8mb4
Recommended Fixes for Your Current Config
Enable binlog expiry: add binlog_expire_logs_seconds = 604800, otherwise disk fills.
Reduce tmp_table_size (2G is dangerous) to 64–256M, and set max_heap_table_size the same.
Reduce bulk_insert_buffer_size to default (8M) unless using MyISAM.
Raise innodb_open_files and add table_open_cache if you have many tables.
Raise innodb_io_capacity if you’re on SSD/NVMe.
Add sync_binlog=1 and innodb_flush_log_at_trx_commit=1 for crash safety.
Add skip-name-resolve, utf8mb4 charset, innodb_file_per_table.
Set read_only/super_read_only = ON if this server is a replica.
Make sure max_connections=1000 is realistic: per-connection buffers × 1000 can exhaust RAM.

Notes

Some parameters (lower_case_table_names, innodb_log_file_size in older versions) must be set before initializing the data directory.
Restart MySQL after editing, and verify with SHOW VARIABLES LIKE 'param_name';.
